§ `s 271`

-- (2) "(a) any release otherwise validly given ...; (b) any provision enabling such a release to be given (i) on the agreement of a majority of not less than three fourths in nominal value of the debenture holders present and voting ...; and (ii) either with respect to specific acts or omissions or on the dissolution of the trustee"
-- arguments: release validly given; provision enables a release; nominal value agreeing; nominal value present and voting; with respect to specific acts, dissolution or ceasing to act
#ASSERT (`s 271(2) subsection (1) does not invalidate the release or the provision` TRUE FALSE 0 0 FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- three fourths: 75 of 100 agree (exactly three fourths), the provision enabling the release is valid
#ASSERT (`s 271(2) subsection (1) does not invalidate the release or the provision` FALSE TRUE 75 100 TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 74 of 100 is below three fourths
#ASSERT (`s 271(2) subsection (1) does not invalidate the release or the provision` FALSE TRUE 74 100 TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- the release is not with respect to specific acts or a dissolution
#ASSERT (`s 271(2) subsection (1) does not invalidate the release or the provision` FALSE TRUE 100 100 FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 271(2) subsection (1) does not invalidate the release or the provision` FALSE FALSE 100 100 TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (3) a provision in force on 29 December 1967 so long as a trustee entitled to it remains a trustee; and a trustee's exemption while it was in force
#ASSERT (`s 271(3) subsection (1) does not operate against the provision or the trustee's exemption` TRUE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 271(3) subsection (1) does not operate against the provision or the trustee's exemption` TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 271(3) subsection (1) does not operate against the provision or the trustee's exemption` FALSE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 271(3) subsection (1) does not operate against the provision or the trustee's exemption` FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (1) void insofar as it would exempt or indemnify the trustee where the trustee fails to show the degree of care and diligence required
-- arguments: in a trust deed or contract; would exempt or indemnify; trustee fails to show care; answer of (2); answer of (3)
#ASSERT (`s 271(1) the provision is void` TRUE TRUE TRUE (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 271(1) the provision is void` TRUE TRUE TRUE NOTHING NOTHING) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 271(1) the provision is void` TRUE TRUE FALSE NOTHING NOTHING) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 271(1) the provision is void` FALSE TRUE TRUE NOTHING NOTHING) EQUALS NOTHING
-- subsection (1) "does not invalidate" what (2) or (3) saves
#ASSERT (`s 271(1) the provision is void` TRUE TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) NOTHING) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 271(1) the provision is void` TRUE TRUE TRUE NOTHING (JUST TRUE)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
